import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 440 | Dragon Ball · God-of-Destruction Setting Critique: Personal Dictatorship of a Cosmos-Tier Being","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 440 | Dragon Ball · God-of-Destruction Setting Critique: Personal Dictatorship of a Cosmos-Tier Being","no":440,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","God of Destruction","Beerus","Dictatorship","Cosmos-Tier","Myriad-Ranks Republicanism"],"related":["49-Governance Framework and Checks-and-Balances","40-Symbiotic Constitution General Outline","05-Myriad-Ranks Co-Progression Program"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0440_模块2-龙珠-破坏神设定批判-宇宙级存在的个人独裁.md","filePath":"en/0440_模块2-龙珠-破坏神设定批判-宇宙级存在的个人独裁.md"}'),s={name:"en/0440_模块2-龙珠-破坏神设定批判-宇宙级存在的个人独裁.md"};function a(r,e,l,c,u,d){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-440-dragon-ball-·-god-of-destruction-setting-critique-personal-dictatorship-of-a-cosmos-tier-being" tabindex="-1">Entry 440 | Dragon Ball · God-of-Destruction Setting Critique: Personal Dictatorship of a Cosmos-Tier Being <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-440-dragon-ball-·-god-of-destruction-setting-critique-personal-dictatorship-of-a-cosmos-tier-being" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 440 | Dragon Ball · God-of-Destruction Setting Critique: Personal Dictatorship of a Cosmos-Tier Being&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 9) | Benchmark base: Documents 49, 40, 05</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-a-god-says-i-m-going-to-sleep" tabindex="-1">Introduction: when a god says &quot;I&#39;m going to sleep&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-a-god-says-i-m-going-to-sleep" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: when a god says &quot;I&#39;m going to sleep&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p><em>Dragon Ball Super</em> introduced the God of Destruction Beerus — the most &quot;politically incorrect&quot; setting in Dragon Ball worldview: a cosmos-tier being capable of casually destroying planets, whose entire job is &quot;decide whether to destroy by mood.&quot; He sleeps when he wants for centuries; when he wakes he finds planets to smash for fun; whoever he dislikes he makes disappear — no council, no law, no term, no appeal. This is not a god; this is a cosmos-tier dictator. This entry, by the law-first axiom and republican axiom of Myriad Races, dissects the God-of-Destruction setting&#39;s institutional lesion.</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The God of Destruction&#39;s energy level is cosmos-tier, but its direction is pure waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Destruction &gt; construction</strong>: Beerus&#39;s entire &quot;job&quot; is destruction; he never used this energy to build any planet, help any race</li><li><strong>Waking = disaster</strong>: every time Beerus wakes, the cosmos tenses; his &quot;daily life&quot; is Myriad Ranks&#39; &quot;disaster countdown&quot;</li><li><strong>Training Goku out of private interest</strong>: Beerus spars with Goku not for cosmos peace, but &quot;find someone fun to fight&quot; — cosmos-tier public resources used for personal entertainment</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How God-of-Destruction dictatorship feeds historical regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Myriad Ranks have no security expectation</strong>: any race does not know whether Beerus will wake tomorrow, will take a fancy to their planet — civilization dares not do long-term construction</li><li><strong>No institutional constraint</strong>: above the God of Destruction only Angels (observers) and Zeno (higher dictator); Myriad Ranks themselves have no constraint channel on the God of Destruction</li><li><strong>Power hereditary/appointed</strong>: God of Destruction chosen as apprentice by previous God of Destruction; Supreme Kais chosen by Supreme Kais — cosmos governance stratum completely closed; Myriad Ranks have no participation right</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku&#39;s predatory thinking in his relationship with the God of Destruction:</p><ul><li><strong>Befriending a dictator as equals</strong>: after Goku beat Beerus, Beerus stopped smashing Earth — this &quot;get-out-of-jail-free card&quot; was bought by Goku&#39;s strength, not by Myriad Ranks&#39; institutions. That is, Earth&#39;s safety depends on whether Goku can keep beating Beerus</li><li><strong>Training resources monopolized</strong>: Whis sparring with Goku is essentially the God-of-Destruction system lending cosmos-tier mentor resources to one Saiyan on Earth — no other being in Myriad Ranks gets this treatment</li><li><strong>Taking dictator as friend</strong>: Goku never questions Beerus&#39;s dictatorial legitimacy, only cares &quot;is it fun to fight him&quot; — this is structural disregard of Myriad Ranks&#39; suffering</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dragon Ball God-of-Destruction Dictatorship</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Governance Framework</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>God of Destruction personally decides planet survival</td><td>Anchor Council legislation: planet survival goes legal process; not tied to one person</td></tr><tr><td>No term, no appeal</td><td>Symbiotic Court judicial independence: Myriad Ranks have appeal right against governors</td></tr><tr><td>Power hereditary, closed</td><td>Myriad Ranks 99% full coverage: any race, any cultivator has qualification to participate in governance</td></tr><tr><td>Destruction &gt; construction</td><td>Collective ascension axiom: strong ones feed back to Myriad Ranks; construction &gt; destruction</td></tr><tr><td>Goku befriends dictator</td><td>Anchor Inspection Committee: supervise all cosmos-tier strong ones, including Goku</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates God-of-Destruction power structure — 12 universes each with God of Destruction + Angel + Supreme Kai</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;if God of Destruction elected by Myriad-Ranks parliament, ten-thousand-year term, with appeal channel&quot; control</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count Myriad-Ranks long-term construction rate, planet-civilization survival years, cosmos-tier disaster frequency</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>God-of-Destruction Dictatorship Institutional Cost Report</em>, quantifying &quot;during Beerus&#39;s four-hundred-year sleep, how many civilizations the cosmos failed to build&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: low</strong>. God of Destruction &quot;destruction maintains cosmos balance&quot; claim never truly executed in plot — Beerus smashes planets mostly &quot;dislike,&quot; unrelated to cosmos balance</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: high</strong>. Super&#39;s &quot;12 universes&quot; setting after Tournament of Power directly wiped 8 by Zeno; universe count changes with plot</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high (gift-style-leaning-oligarchic)</strong>. Earth safety relies on Goku&#39;s private relationship with Beerus, not institutional guarantee</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: cosmos-tier energy all used for destruction and personal entertainment</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: Myriad Ranks&#39; planets and lives disposed of at the God of Destruction&#39;s whim</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least did not become a dictator; Beerus is institutionalized dictatorship</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Myriad Ranks have no constraint channel on the God of Destruction</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: 12 universes should have been multigovernance&#39;s rich ore, but written as 12 dictators&#39; fiefs</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The God-of-Destruction setting&#39;s appearance marks Dragon Ball worldview&#39;s upgrade from &quot;Earth martial arts&quot; to &quot;cosmos politics&quot; — but the direction it upgraded was higher-grade dictatorship, not higher-grade republic. What Heng Yuan Zhou wants to ask: if a cosmos-tier being can decide a planet&#39;s survival, why should Myriad Ranks not fear? Dragon Ball&#39;s answer is &quot;luckily Goku can beat him&quot; — this is not an answer, this is a bigger problem.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · God-of-Destruction setting critique · personal dictatorship of a cosmos-tier being described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./441_模块2-龙珠-天使设定批判-更高层级的恩赐制.html">Entry 441 · Angel Setting</a> · <a href="./442_模块2-龙珠-全王设定批判-终极存在的随意性.html">Entry 442 · Zeno Setting</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/49-治理框架与权力制衡.html">49-Governance Framework and Checks-and-Balances</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const m=t(s,[["render",a]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
